about 10% above forecast looks best.\n\n**Candidates:**\n- **Candidate 0:** the plan has 26 pairs instead of the required 30, so it is likely invalid. Its quantities are also uneven.\n- **Candidate 1:** orders every 2 days at about 1.1 × forecast. This is a good level, and batching costs about nothing.\n- **Candidate 2:** orders exactly the forecast, which is below the 1.046 average demand. It will run short every day.\n- **Candidate 3:** orders daily at about 1.17 × forecast. It carries noticeable surplus, but it is still decent.\n- **Candidate 4:** orders product 0 at about 1.22 × forecast (cheap surplus) but product 1, the higher-margin product, at only about 1.05 × forecast. It is borderline.\n- **Candidate 5:** orders daily at about 1.1 × forecast, the best level.\n- **Candidate 6:** orders every 2 days at about 1.2 × forecast. Expensive product 1 overstock builds up and risks overflow.\n- **Candidate 7:** orders every 3 days, so it carries extra holding cost. Its arrivals of about 175 units on top of carried-over stock risk overflowing the warehouse.\n\nThe order of the 4th and 5th places (candidates 4 and 6) is the least certain."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5026, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 5026}, "output_tokens": 2, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T08:44:11.746Z", "request_id": "req_011CgWERv7io8d64h4oQK3XY"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_0164usKjKJAHjVnQTd2HknxT", "name": "Structu